      "id": "verbosity_explain_water",
      "category": "verbosity_fingerprint",
      "check_type": "length_range",
      "passed": false,
      "errored": false,
      "error": null,
      "latency_ms": 2770.2,
      "prompt_tokens": 11,
      "completion_tokens": 587,
      "output": "At its most fundamental level, **water** is a chemical compound made up of two types of atoms: hydrogen and oxygen. Its chemical formula is **$\\text{H}_2\\text{O}$**—meaning every single molecule of water consists of two hydrogen atoms bonded to one oxygen atom. \n\nHowever, to humans, Earth, and life itself, water is much more than a simple chemical formula. Here is a breakdown of what water is through different lenses:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Physical and Chemical Properties\nWater is famous for being uniquely weird and wonderful in the world of physics and chemistry:\n* **The Three States:** Water is the only natural substance on Earth that exists abundantly in three physical states: **liquid** (oceans, rivers), **solid** (ice, snow), and **gas** (steam, vapor).\n* **The \"Universal Solvent\":** Because of its chemical structure (it is a \"polar\" molecule, meaning one side has a slight positive charge and the other a slight negative charge), water can dissolve more substances than any other liquid. This is why it carries vital nutrients in our bodies and minerals in the earth.\n* **Density Anomaly:** Most substances shrink and become denser when they freeze. Water actually *expands* and becomes less dense when it turns to ice. This is why ice floats, which prevents lakes and oceans from freezing solid from the bottom up, allowing aquatic life to survive the winter.\n* **High Heat Capacity:** Water can absorb a lot of heat before its temperature changes significantly. This helps regulate the climate of the entire planet and keeps our body temperatures stable.\n\n### 2. The Driver of Life\nBiologically, water is the cradle of life. \n* All known life depends on it. The human body is made up of about 60% water, and the brain is roughly 73% water. \n* It acts as a medium for metabolic and cellular processes, flushes out toxins, regulates body temperature, and cushions our organs and joints.\n\n### 3. Earth’s Lifeblood\nWater shapes our planet more than any other force.\n* **Global Coverage:** About 71% of the Earth's surface is covered by water, mostly in the oceans (which hold about 96.5% of all Earth's water).\n* **The Water Cycle:** Water is endlessly recycled through the Earth in a closed system known as the hydrological cycle. It evaporates from the oceans, forms clouds, falls as rain or snow (precipitation), flows through rivers, and returns to the sea. \n\n### Summary\nWater is the ultimate connector. It is the fluid that lubricates the mechanics of living organisms, the sculptors of landscapes, the thermostat of the planet, and the simple, transparent molecule without which life as we know it could not exist."
